## Updated Fix

After testing, here's the complete fix:

### Root Cause
The model lookup was correctly finding models, but when users specify models like `groq/compound` (with a slash), the API call needs to use the full model ID including the provider prefix.

### Solution

**1. In config, models that need the full prefix should define `id`:**

```json
{
  "providers": {
    "groq": {
      "models": {
        "compound": {
          "id": "groq/compound",  // Full model ID
          "name": "Groq Compound"
        },
        "compound-mini": {
          "id": "groq/compound-mini",
          "name": "Groq Compound Mini"
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**2. The code fix (in `packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts`):**

The `getModel` function already handles this correctly - it uses the configured `api.id` from the model config.

### Test Results

| Model | Status |
|-------|--------|
| groq/compound | ✅ Found, API called correctly |
| groq/llama-3.1-8b-instant | ✅ Works (backward compatible) |
| cerebras/llama3.1-8b | ✅ Works |

The fix allows models like `groq/compound` to work while maintaining backward compatibility with existing models.
